-- title:
--   Nonnegative order propagates to elements integral over K[j]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ an algebra over $K$, and let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$ in the sense of the project: a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$ under the structure map, distinct from all of $F$, and whose ring is a principal ideal ring. For $f \in F$ the order $v.\mathrm{ord}\, f$ is the integer obtained as the negative of the `WithZero` logarithm of the value of $f$ under the $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation attached to the height-one prime determined by $v$. The hypotheses are two elements $j, u \in F$ such that $u$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra $\mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\,K\,\{j\}$ of $F$ generated by $j$, i.e. $u$ satisfies a monic polynomial equation with coefficients in that subalgebra, and such that $0 \le v.\mathrm{ord}\, j$. The conclusion is that $0 \le v.\mathrm{ord}\, u$.
--
--   This is the valuative form of the statement that the integral closure of a valuation ring is contained in that ring when the ring is integrally closed: nonnegativity of the order at a place passes from $j$ to every element integral over $K[j]$. It is used throughout the treatment of places on curves, for instance in the analysis of regular prolongations and in the integrality arguments for forms modulo $p$ expressed in terms of the $j$-invariant.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ord_nonneg_of_isIntegral_adjoin_of_ord_nonneg.lean

